      "eventIntro": "In 1434, Jan van Eyck painted a double portrait filled with reflective surfaces, textiles, gestures, inscriptions, and carefully observed objects. The painting uses oil technique to make social life appear materially dense and symbolically charged.",
      "eventIntroZh": "1434 年，扬·范艾克绘制了一幅充满反射表面、织物、手势、题记和细致物件的双人肖像。它利用油画技术，让社会生活显得物质密集并带有象征意味。",
      "whyMatters": "The work became a touchstone for Northern Renaissance painting because it showed how oil could render light, texture, identity, and domestic setting with unusual precision.",
