      "titleZh": "杜尚提交《泉》",
      "summary": "Duchamp's Fountain turned selection, context, authorship, and institutional framing into central questions for modern art.",
      "summaryZh": "杜尚的《泉》把选择、语境、作者身份和制度框架变成现代艺术的核心问题。",
      "eventIntro": "In 1917, Marcel Duchamp submitted a signed urinal titled Fountain to the Society of Independent Artists in New York. Its rejection exposed the limits of supposedly open exhibition rules and made the readymade a provocation.",
      "eventIntroZh": "1917 年，马塞尔·杜尚向纽约独立艺术家协会提交了一个署名为《泉》的小便池。它被拒绝，暴露出所谓开放展览规则的边界，也让现成品成为挑衅。",
      "whyMatters": "Fountain mattered because it shifted attention from hand-made form to decision, naming, display, and institutional authority. It changed what later artists could ask an artwork to be.",
      "whyMattersZh": "《泉》重要，因为它把注意力从手工形式转向决定、命名、展示和制度权威。它改变了后来艺术家对“艺术品可以是什么”的提问方式。",
      "phaseRelation": "It belongs to Modern painting and abstraction broadly because the modernist break included not only abstraction, but also attacks on medium, authorship, and taste.",
      "phaseRelationZh": "它广义上属于“现代绘画与抽象”阶段，因为现代主义断裂不仅包括抽象，也包括对媒介、作者身份和品味的攻击。",
      "connectionHint": "It connects to conceptual art, museum critique, design objects, commodity culture, and later digital debates over originality and reproducibility.",
      "connectionHintZh": "它连接到观念艺术、博物馆批判、设计物品、商品文化，以及后来数字时代关于原创性和可复制性的争论。",
