      "titleZh": "马列维奇展出《黑方块》",
      "summary": "Black Square made abstraction appear as a radical zero point, rejecting representational painting for a new pictorial and philosophical language.",
      "summaryZh": "《黑方块》让抽象成为激进的零点，拒绝再现绘画，提出新的图像与哲学语言。",
      "eventIntro": "In 1915, Kazimir Malevich exhibited Black Square in Petrograd at The Last Futurist Exhibition of Paintings 0,10. Hung high in a corner, it echoed the position of an icon while refusing recognizable religious or natural imagery.",
      "eventIntroZh": "1915 年，卡济米尔·马列维奇在彼得格勒“最后的未来主义绘画展 0,10”中展出《黑方块》。它被高挂在角落，呼应圣像位置，却拒绝任何可识别的宗教或自然图像。",
      "whyMatters": "The painting mattered because it made abstraction a total program rather than a stylistic variation. It asked viewers to treat surface, geometry, and idea as sufficient artistic content.",
      "whyMattersZh": "这幅画重要，因为它把抽象变成完整纲领，而不只是风格变化。它要求观者把表面、几何和观念本身视为足够的艺术内容。",
      "phaseRelation": "It belongs to Modern painting and abstraction because it shows painting breaking from depiction into systems of form, ideology, and avant-garde manifesto.",
