      "id": "event-daguerreotype-announced-1839",
      "year": 1839,
      "title": "Daguerreotype process announced",
      "titleZh": "银版摄影法公布",
      "summary": "The public announcement of the daguerreotype made photography a practical public technology for fixing images made by light.",
      "summaryZh": "银版摄影法的公开宣布，让摄影成为一种用光固定图像的实际公共技术。",
      "eventIntro": "In 1839, the French state announced Louis Daguerre's photographic process to the public. The daguerreotype produced detailed images on silvered plates and quickly drew scientific, artistic, commercial, and popular attention.",
      "eventIntroZh": "1839 年，法国政府向公众公布路易·达盖尔的摄影方法。银版摄影能在镀银板上生成细节丰富的图像，很快吸引科学、艺术、商业和大众兴趣。",
      "whyMatters": "The announcement matters because it made photography a public medium almost immediately. Portrait studios, scientific documentation, urban views, colonial records, and family memory all changed around chemical images.",
      "whyMattersZh": "这次公布重要，因为它几乎立刻让摄影成为公共媒介。肖像馆、科学记录、城市景观、殖民档案和家庭记忆都围绕化学图像发生变化。",
      "phaseRelation": "It belongs to Daguerreotype and early photographic studios because it marks photography's transition from experiment to public practice.",
      "phaseRelationZh": "它属于“银版摄影与早期照相馆”阶段，因为它标志摄影从实验转向公共实践。",
      "connectionHint": "It connects to industrial chemistry, portrait commerce, state patronage, visual evidence, and later arguments over whether photography was art or technology.",
      "connectionHintZh": "它连接到工业化学、肖像商业、国家赞助、视觉证据，以及后来关于摄影是艺术还是技术的争论。",
