      "titleZh": "塔尔博特获得卡罗式摄影法专利",
      "summary": "The calotype introduced a negative-positive photographic process that made reproducible paper photographs central to photography's future.",
      "summaryZh": "卡罗式摄影法引入负片—正片流程，让可复制的纸基照片成为摄影未来的核心。",
      "eventIntro": "In 1841, William Henry Fox Talbot patented the calotype in Britain. Unlike a unique daguerreotype plate, the calotype used a paper negative from which multiple positive prints could be made.",
      "eventIntroZh": "1841 年，威廉·亨利·福克斯·塔尔博特在英国为卡罗式摄影法申请专利。不同于唯一的银版照片，卡罗式使用纸质负片，可以制作多个正片。",
      "whyMatters": "The process mattered because it pointed photography toward reproducibility, albums, archives, publishing, and later film-based image culture.",
      "whyMattersZh": "这一方法重要，因为它把摄影推向可复制性、相册、档案、出版以及后来的胶片图像文化。",
      "phaseRelation": "It belongs to the Daguerreotype and early photographic studios phase, but it represents a different future: photography as repeatable paper image rather than singular metal plate.",
      "phaseRelationZh": "它属于“银版摄影与早期照相馆”阶段，但代表另一种未来：摄影作为可重复的纸上图像，而不是唯一金属板。",
