      "eventIntroZh": "2008 年，Casey Reas 和 Ben Fry 开发多年的 Processing 1.0 发布。这个项目提供了一种通过绘图、动画、互动和视觉系统学习编程的语言与环境。",
      "whyMatters": "Processing mattered because it lowered the threshold for artists and designers to work directly with code. It helped normalize programming as a material for visual culture rather than only an engineering skill.",
      "whyMattersZh": "Processing 重要，因为它降低了艺术家和设计师直接使用代码的门槛。它帮助把编程常态化为视觉文化材料，而不只是工程技能。",
      "phaseRelation": "It belongs to Social media, platforms, and post-internet art only partly; more importantly it bridges interactive multimedia, internet communities, and creative coding education.",
      "phaseRelationZh": "它部分属于“社交媒体、平台与后互联网艺术”，但更重要的是连接互动多媒体、互联网社群和创意编程教育。",
      "connectionHint": "It connects to software education, generative art, data visualization, maker culture, and later p5.js browser-based creative coding.",
      "connectionHintZh": "它连接到软件教育、生成艺术、数据可视化、创客文化，以及后来基于浏览器的 p5.js 创意编程。",
