      "title": "ILOVEYOU worm spreads globally",
      "titleZh": "ILOVEYOU 蠕虫全球传播",
      "summary": "The ILOVEYOU worm spread through email attachments in 2000, showing how social engineering and connected office software could create global security incidents.",
      "summaryZh": "ILOVEYOU 蠕虫在 2000 年通过电子邮件附件传播，显示社交工程和互联办公软件如何制造全球安全事件。",
      "eventIntro": "In May 2000, an email with the subject line ILOVEYOU carried a malicious attachment that rapidly infected computers around the world. Its spread relied less on technical sophistication than on trust, curiosity, and weak default software behavior.",
      "eventIntroZh": "2000 年 5 月，一封主题为 ILOVEYOU 的邮件携带恶意附件，迅速感染世界各地计算机。它的传播与其说依赖高深技术，不如说依赖信任、好奇心和软件默认行为的脆弱性。",
      "whyMatters": "ILOVEYOU made cybersecurity feel like an everyday social and organizational problem. Email, scripting, address books, and office networks became attack surfaces, not just communication tools.",
      "whyMattersZh": "ILOVEYOU 让网络安全显得像一个日常社会与组织问题。电子邮件、脚本、通讯录和办公网络不再只是沟通工具，也成为攻击面。",
      "phaseRelation": "This event belongs to the malware, botnets, and cybercrime phase because it showed how mass connectivity could turn small malicious code into global disruption.",
