      "eventIntro": "Unix development began at Bell Labs in 1969 as a smaller, more flexible response to large time-sharing systems. It favored simple tools, files as interfaces, and a programming environment built for developers.",
      "eventIntroZh": "Unix 于 1969 年在贝尔实验室开始开发，是对大型分时系统的一种更小、更灵活的回应。它偏好简单工具、以文件作为接口，以及面向开发者的编程环境。",
      "whyMatters": "Unix became less important as a single product than as a software lineage. Its ideas shaped BSD, Linux, macOS, servers, internet infrastructure, shell culture, and the way programmers think about composable tools.",
      "whyMattersZh": "Unix 作为单一产品的重要性不如作为软件谱系的重要性。它的理念影响 BSD、Linux、macOS、服务器、互联网基础设施、shell 文化，以及程序员对可组合工具的理解。",
      "phaseRelation": "This event anchors the Unix, C, and portable software phase because Unix made operating systems feel like portable programming environments rather than machine-specific control software.",
